WEBVTT

00:00.095 --> 00:05.533
As for the dream-filled Tomorrow,

00:05.867 --> 00:11.134
No one can see it.

00:13.241 --> 00:18.679
I close my eyes and think of you,

00:19.347 --> 00:25.115
Who I'll meet someday.

00:25.553 --> 00:31.719
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:32.093 --> 00:38.362
Show the spring to these eyes of mine.

00:38.666 --> 00:44.866
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:45.240 --> 00:51.304
Farewell to the city in winter.

00:51.746 --> 00:57.981
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:58.286 --> 01:04.589
Call the spring to my heart.

01:04.859 --> 01:11.230
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

01:11.533 --> 01:18.029
Farewell, snow flakes.

01:41.062 --> 01:43.155
The cause of the fire
has not yet been determined.

01:43.431 --> 01:44.693
Is that so?

01:45.133 --> 01:47.302
The mage action was
performed as requested.

01:47.302 --> 01:49.065
And after requests
are fulfilled, well...

01:50.772 --> 01:52.106
Kikuchi Yume-san?

01:52.106 --> 01:52.765
Yes.

01:56.477 --> 01:58.446
Regarding your certification exam...

01:58.446 --> 01:59.881
Yes.

01:59.881 --> 02:05.615
Your assignment is to use your
Special Power on Oyamada Masami-san.

02:06.120 --> 02:07.188
What?

02:07.188 --> 02:08.177
Master Chief!

02:08.723 --> 02:10.925
Trainee Kikuchi Yume-san...

02:10.925 --> 02:15.794
will use her Special Power on
Instructor Oyamada Masami-san.

02:16.831 --> 02:20.289
This is to be
your certification exam.

02:28.576 --> 02:31.568
I'll use my Special Power
on Sensei?

02:32.447 --> 02:34.108
What kind of Special Power
should I use?

02:35.216 --> 02:38.413
That's something
you have to decide for yourself.

02:38.987 --> 02:40.818
Me...

02:41.289 --> 02:44.692
You just received your topic
from Master Chief Ginpun, right?

02:44.692 --> 02:47.923
So it's you who
needs to arrange it.

02:48.830 --> 02:53.392
"A Broken Rainbow"

02:53.968 --> 02:56.604
This is an announcement from
the Central Information Bureau...

02:56.604 --> 02:59.540
for those mages
that are standing by.

02:59.540 --> 03:01.175
If you're here to attend
the monthly meeting,

03:01.175 --> 03:04.212
please come to
Conference Room #2.

03:04.212 --> 03:06.915
Once again...
This is an announcement from...
This was a tough
case for you, wasn't it?

03:06.915 --> 03:12.182
I'm sure it was a shock that the fire
happened the day of your mage action.

03:14.889 --> 03:17.483
But it's not your fault,
Yume-chan.

03:18.126 --> 03:21.152
Don't worry about it.
Cheer up.

03:23.164 --> 03:25.166
Um... Endo-san?

03:25.166 --> 03:25.962
Hmm?

03:28.469 --> 03:32.371
I'd like to visit
Takahashi-san in the hospital.

03:32.540 --> 03:34.235
Do you know
which hospital she's in?

03:35.977 --> 03:42.382
Oyamada-sensei, I'm sorry,
but I want to apologize to her.

03:46.220 --> 03:47.209
Yume-chan...

03:48.556 --> 03:54.562
If... If I had listened better,
there might have been another way.

03:54.562 --> 03:58.362
If you know which hospital
she's in, please tell me. Please.

04:13.147 --> 04:13.848
Excuse me.

04:13.848 --> 04:14.849
Yes.

04:14.849 --> 04:17.841
Um... Which room is
Takahashi-san in?

04:18.720 --> 04:22.713
Let's see...
Takahashi Mitsuko-san, right?

04:23.057 --> 04:24.388
Are you a family member?

04:24.792 --> 04:26.350
No. Um...

04:27.261 --> 04:32.255
Right now only family
is allowed to see her.

04:32.934 --> 04:34.492
What do you mean?

04:34.902 --> 04:36.927
She's in critical condition.

04:37.939 --> 04:39.566
Critical condition?

04:41.175 --> 04:43.077
Uh, excuse me...

04:43.077 --> 04:46.774
Could you give
these flowers to her?

04:47.315 --> 04:48.782
Sure. I'll be happy to.

04:55.256 --> 04:57.349
I regret making the request...

05:18.980 --> 05:20.538
I thought you were a ghost.

05:21.649 --> 05:22.707
Yume.

05:40.835 --> 05:43.929
Do you think
my mage action was wrong?

05:44.572 --> 05:48.099
If it was performed as requested,
there's no problem.

05:49.010 --> 05:52.707
Angela, you don't care what happens
after you use Special Power?

05:53.014 --> 05:57.610
I always do my best, so I don't
think about what happens later.

05:58.586 --> 06:02.613
You don't think about whether or not
your Special Power was useful?

06:03.024 --> 06:06.323
Special Power
is undoubtedly useful.

06:12.033 --> 06:14.024
Your exam...
Isn't it tomorrow?

06:14.669 --> 06:15.693
Yeah.

06:16.137 --> 06:19.538
As soon as my suspension expires,
I have to take my exam, too.

06:21.776 --> 06:22.543
Here is fine.

06:22.543 --> 06:24.204
Thank you for
the tea and sweets.

06:27.782 --> 06:29.750
Shimo-Kitazawa
Shopping Street

06:31.752 --> 06:32.987
- Oh, how fun!

06:32.987 --> 06:34.147
- Oh, how fun!
- Let's go!

06:35.056 --> 06:36.257
- Sounds good!

06:36.257 --> 06:37.825
- Sounds good!
- I can't wait!

06:37.825 --> 06:39.026
- That store's great!

06:39.026 --> 06:40.516
- That store's great!
- Way cool!

06:51.405 --> 06:52.463
Here you go.

06:59.947 --> 07:02.040
Ah! Oh, well...

07:02.250 --> 07:06.016
That outfit...
Are you a mage?

07:06.187 --> 07:07.176
Yes.

07:07.421 --> 07:12.120
Well! If you're a mage, at least
do something about a kid's balloon.

07:13.427 --> 07:15.029
Ah, come on!

07:15.029 --> 07:17.725
When this kid starts to cry,
she won't stop.

07:19.267 --> 07:20.256
Stop crying!

07:21.002 --> 07:23.994
I'm sorry.
I apologize.

07:25.039 --> 07:27.030
Huh! What a phony!

07:27.642 --> 07:29.633
That's not... I'm...

07:30.111 --> 07:31.772
Let's go!

07:51.966 --> 07:56.130
It's time you cut
your ties with Takako!

07:58.806 --> 08:03.334
That you can't forget her can't be
helped. But, as for being bound...

08:04.445 --> 08:06.470
I am responsible.

08:06.814 --> 08:11.251
No, you're not. Not at all!
That was just an accident.

08:12.386 --> 08:16.186
No, it wasn't.
I killed Takako.

08:16.324 --> 08:17.313
Killed?

08:19.827 --> 08:24.662
No! It's not what you think!
Yume, don't believe him!

08:26.167 --> 08:27.532
It's true.

08:28.169 --> 08:31.539
Masami-chan,
you've never killed anyone!

08:31.539 --> 08:34.167
That... No one could've
done anything about that.

08:37.011 --> 08:38.279
That time...

08:38.279 --> 08:42.583
I should have been the one to do
something, because I'm a mage.

08:42.583 --> 08:45.353
But I could do nothing...

08:45.353 --> 08:47.048
I can't do anything, either.

08:48.189 --> 08:51.317
I'm not useful to anyone.

08:51.726 --> 08:54.559
I just hurt people's feelings,
and people don't like me, and...

08:55.529 --> 08:56.655
Yume-chan...

08:57.198 --> 09:01.430
Although Zennosuke-san's leg
is better, he's not playing soccer!

09:01.535 --> 09:04.868
The windows at that shopping
district have scratches everywhere,

09:05.206 --> 09:08.232
and Mitsuko-san regrets
making the request.

09:09.277 --> 09:12.303
She's still in critical condition, and...

09:24.225 --> 09:25.214
Yume.

09:37.905 --> 09:41.238
What will I do if
Mitsuko-san can't be saved?

09:44.078 --> 09:48.708
I don't want to use
Special Power anymore!

09:49.884 --> 09:54.344
It's like Oyamada-sensei said:
"Special Power is not almighty."

09:54.822 --> 09:56.255
It's like Oyamada-sensei said...

10:03.097 --> 10:06.760
You're just like Masami-chan...
ten years ago.

10:13.107 --> 10:15.598
Me...
ten years ago...

10:40.835 --> 10:41.824
Yume-chan...

11:23.944 --> 11:25.746
My suntan is starting to hurt!

11:25.746 --> 11:28.306
Did you bring a long-sleeved
jacket or something?

11:28.716 --> 11:29.517
No.

11:29.517 --> 11:31.485
Then do you
want to wear my shirt?

11:31.852 --> 11:34.116
Oh, yes! I get to wear
Masami-kun's shirt!

12:00.614 --> 12:02.047
Takako!

12:02.783 --> 12:04.944
Takako! Takako!

12:07.388 --> 12:11.552
You're all right. I can heal these wounds
with my Special Power.

12:21.402 --> 12:22.426
Takako, hang in there!

12:24.138 --> 12:25.230
Ugh...

12:25.739 --> 12:29.539
Takako! That's right.
Keep your eyes open!

12:30.711 --> 12:32.235
I'll help you right away.

12:32.713 --> 12:34.977
I can heal
these little wounds quickly!

12:36.750 --> 12:39.048
It's all right.
I'm with you.

12:40.921 --> 12:41.910
Takako?

12:43.424 --> 12:46.594
Th... ank... you...

12:46.594 --> 12:48.596
I can't hear you.

12:48.596 --> 12:50.188
Don't talk now!

12:50.798 --> 12:53.323
I'll help you right away.
Right away!

13:01.108 --> 13:02.097
Takako?

13:04.445 --> 13:06.436
Takako!

13:06.580 --> 13:08.673
Takako!

13:08.849 --> 13:11.044
TAKAKO!

13:20.461 --> 13:24.124
I couldn't save Takako.

13:31.505 --> 13:37.705
If you can't save a life with Special Power,
then why do I have such power?

13:38.879 --> 13:40.814
I've thought about it
a long time.

13:40.814 --> 13:44.807
That's why you shouldn't get attached to
mage actions you've already completed.

13:45.319 --> 13:48.482
Because then you can't distinguish
your mage actions from your personal life.

13:52.092 --> 13:55.129
Takako loved these flowers.

13:55.129 --> 13:59.156
Masami-chan is
still in love with Takako.

13:59.667 --> 14:05.333
I haven't forgotten Takako, either.
But I'm not bound by her.

14:13.347 --> 14:16.805
It's too much. Special Power
is just too much for me...

14:19.853 --> 14:20.945
Hey, Yume!

14:23.490 --> 14:25.151
Going shopping, Yume?

14:26.527 --> 14:31.089
Good morning!
Huh? What's wrong?

14:32.166 --> 14:33.463
Nothing really.

14:33.701 --> 14:36.067
Good morning.
Thanks for your hard work again.

14:38.606 --> 14:41.803
You're hurting yourself,
all for Yume.

14:44.878 --> 14:46.213
I don't get hurt.

14:46.213 --> 14:49.478
No matter what,
my feelings won't be affected.

14:52.720 --> 14:57.214
You liar! You hurt every time
you use Special Power...

15:03.197 --> 15:05.131
Hello, Bureau of Mage Labor.

15:05.599 --> 15:07.567
I'm Kikuchi, a trainee.

15:08.068 --> 15:11.672
Um, well...
is Master Chief Ginpun in?

15:11.672 --> 15:13.572
Please hold a moment.

15:17.111 --> 15:19.443
Master Chief is
already gone for the day.

15:19.813 --> 15:21.007
Home?

15:24.952 --> 15:26.020
- Yume-san!

15:26.020 --> 15:27.351
- Yume-san!
- Ah, Runa-chan!

15:27.521 --> 15:30.547
What's this?
You're frowning!

15:31.091 --> 15:33.525
Did Good OI' Oyamada
scold you or somethin'?

15:34.128 --> 15:37.529
No. I'm in a hurry.
See you later.

15:40.934 --> 15:43.061
Changed?
You mean Masami-chan?

15:44.405 --> 15:48.933
That's right. Since Yume came,
Boss has become more human.

15:49.276 --> 15:50.641
More human?

15:51.612 --> 15:53.614
Even though
Yume is a handful,

15:53.614 --> 15:55.878
he seems to have
enjoyed himself a lot.

15:58.552 --> 16:00.679
I need to talk to
Master Chief Ginpun.

16:04.825 --> 16:05.883
Please come in.

16:17.805 --> 16:19.534
Please have a seat.

16:21.141 --> 16:23.473
Um, I...

16:25.479 --> 16:28.471
I've become
afraid of Special Power.

16:29.149 --> 16:32.277
I don't want to use
Special Power.

16:41.228 --> 16:45.289
I was conceited to think
that I was useful to others.

16:46.633 --> 16:49.336
If I could relate to
the applicants' feelings,

16:49.336 --> 16:52.673
I thought I could use
Special Power better.

16:52.673 --> 16:57.076
But people's feelings
are not that simple.

17:00.247 --> 17:02.850
People who request a mage action
are often desperate.

17:02.850 --> 17:06.581
If I use Special Power,
I could hurt them even more...

17:08.021 --> 17:11.225
or even change their lives.

17:11.225 --> 17:15.753
I can't use such Special Power
anymore. I'm afraid.

17:21.435 --> 17:23.937
Master Chief Ginpun,
please tell me...

17:23.937 --> 17:25.734
What should I do?

17:31.044 --> 17:33.069
I cannot tell you.

17:35.115 --> 17:39.711
Unless you find the answer
for yourself, it's meaningless.

17:48.228 --> 17:51.254
Master said you could
spend the night here.

17:54.101 --> 17:55.090
See you.

17:58.639 --> 18:00.197
Yume went home.

18:00.574 --> 18:01.905
Is that so?

18:19.459 --> 18:20.460
Who, Yume?

18:20.460 --> 18:22.758
Something was definitely wrong!

18:23.864 --> 18:25.855
Did Yume get home safely?

18:26.200 --> 18:27.258
What do you mean?

18:28.435 --> 18:29.766
I'm a little concerned.

18:33.106 --> 18:34.300
Is Yume here?

18:34.441 --> 18:35.430
I'll go check.

18:37.077 --> 18:38.271
Yume-chan, I'm coming in.

18:45.986 --> 18:47.977
Ok, I'll take Runa home.

18:48.455 --> 18:49.752
Thank you.

18:50.157 --> 18:52.455
Yume-san will be back soon.

18:53.060 --> 18:53.958
I know.

18:56.029 --> 18:56.697
- Runa.

18:56.697 --> 18:58.528
- Runa.
- All right.

19:02.302 --> 19:04.793
Shibuya Station

19:57.190 --> 20:01.183
Are you a sibling
or a boyfriend?

20:01.561 --> 20:04.758
See? Your friend is
right here. Hang in there.

20:12.639 --> 20:14.207
What should I do?

20:14.207 --> 20:17.040
Hang in there!
Hold on!

20:17.711 --> 20:20.271
No, don't! Don't die!

20:22.282 --> 20:24.546
I'm asking you...

20:34.394 --> 20:36.885
Listen, mage!
Don't pity me, mage!

20:38.699 --> 20:41.896
He's gotta be playing
around somewhere!

20:44.905 --> 20:48.966
I guess mage actions don't provide
the fundamental solutions to problems.

20:49.076 --> 20:51.567
I regret making the request...

20:52.045 --> 20:54.878
You can't save one's life
with Special Power.

21:20.207 --> 21:26.703
When I turn around, it's still there,

21:29.750 --> 21:36.246
The future I've been pursuing.

21:38.025 --> 21:47.093
I have something precious in my heart.

21:47.300 --> 21:52.328
Upon the still unseen blue and

21:52.873 --> 21:59.574
The floating clouds, I wished...

22:02.682 --> 22:04.582
Under the Blue Sky

22:04.885 --> 22:11.791
From that dream that we dreamed that day,

22:12.059 --> 22:18.555
Let's not wake up, and let's not stop...

22:21.501 --> 22:23.628
Under the Blue Sky

22:23.804 --> 22:30.573
Let's keep shining and moving on.

22:30.811 --> 22:37.114
The endless journey continues...

22:49.763 --> 22:51.754
PREVIEW

22:53.867 --> 22:55.669
Person to person...

22:55.669 --> 22:57.534
Heart to heart...

22:58.038 --> 22:59.539
Joy...

22:59.539 --> 23:01.374
Anger...

23:01.374 --> 23:03.376
Sorrow...

23:03.376 --> 23:05.445
Happiness...

23:05.445 --> 23:08.505
Everything leads to tomorrow.

23:08.982 --> 23:11.974
Under this blue sky...

23:12.119 --> 23:14.754
The next episode, the last episode,
is "What Is Important to Mages."

23:14.754 --> 23:16.656
"What Is Important to Mages"
The next episode, the last episode,
is "What Is Important to Mages."

23:16.656 --> 23:19.523
"What Is Important to Mages"
I hope you look forward to it!
